<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70413" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεότης</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέο-τας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ητος</span>, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>youth,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ νεότητος . . ἐς γῆρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.86
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Marc.</u>
				10.20
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτέμβονται νεότητος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.445
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρατὴν γὰρ ἀπωλέσαμεν
			νεότητα,</span> i.e. we died young, <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				89
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				637
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				149
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν νεότατι, ἐπὶ
			νεότητος,</span> in one's <i>youth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				12.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				1199
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ach.</u>
				214
			</span></i>: in pl., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ν. ἄφρονες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.359
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Posidipp.
			</span></i> or <i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
			</span></i> or Crates); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ ν.
			ῥωμαλέαι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				360
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Metrod.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>youthful spirit, impetuosity,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.13
			</span></i>: in bad sense, <i>youthful folly, insolence,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκολασίᾳ καὶ ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					26e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. καὶ ἄνοια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					2.7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> collective, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεολαία</span>
			, <i>body of youth,</i> esp. of military or athletic age,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				8(7).75
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				4.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				9.12
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				20
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in
			Crete, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεότας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁ,</span> acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεότα,</span> gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεότας,</span>
			<i>board of officials representing the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέοι</span> (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.1
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				5012.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				525.9
			</span></i> (Gortyn, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
